from tnx import *
def T(iy,iyn,*a): TA(10,iy,iyn,*a)
I1="Iyal 1: Language and Humanity (மொழி, மனிதம்)"
T(1,I1,"annai-mozhiye","Annai Mozhiye (அன்னை மொழியே)",
 "A poet speaks to the mother tongue as to a beloved mother.",
 "Annai Mozhiye is a memorisation poem in which the poet addresses Tamil as mother, calling her the beautiful classical Tamil. It praises the glory, age and sweetness of the language.",
 "The poem teaches love and loyalty to the mother tongue and reminds us that a language is our identity.",
 "Terms: அன்னை (mother), மொழி (language), செந்தமிழ் (refined Tamil) and போற்றுதல் (praise). Learn the poem by heart with its meaning.",
 ["அன்னை","மொழி","செந்தமிழ்","போற்றுதல்","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("The poem praises English.",["It praises Tamil.","Tamil is called mother."]),
 ["m|The poet addresses|the Tamil language|a river|a king|He calls Tamil mother.","m|அன்னை means|mother|father|sister|Mother.","t|It is a memorisation poem.|T|Yes.","m|செந்தமிழ் means|pure Tamil|slang|English|Refined Tamil.","s|What does மொழி mean?|language|Language.","t|The poem teaches love for the mother tongue.|T|Yes."])
T(1,I1,"pavanar-tamil-sol-valam","Pavanar Parvaiyil Thamizhch-chol Valam (பாவாணர் பார்வையில் தமிழ்ச்சொல் வளம்)",
 "Tamil has survived when many languages have faded.",
 "This prose lesson begins with Bharathiyar's line that country and language are our two eyes. It says that Tamil has swum through the flood of time while many languages have melted away, and that it has so many special qualities that one wonders what richness it lacks.",
 "The lesson looks at Tamil word wealth through the eyes of Devaneya Pavanar, who showed that Tamil words are rich, root-based and descriptive.",
 "Terms: சொல்வளம் (word wealth), வேர்ச்சொல் (root word), மொழி and பாவாணர். Learn examples of how roots give rise to many words.",
 ["சொல்வளம்","வேர்ச்சொல்","பாவாணர்","மொழி","தமிழ்"],
 ("Tamil has few words.",["Tamil has rich word wealth.","Pavanar showed its roots."]),
 ["m|Bharathiyar called country and language our|two eyes|two hands|two houses|Two eyes.","m|Pavanar studied|Tamil word wealth|chemistry|trade|Sol valam.","t|Tamil has survived through the ages.|T|Yes.","m|வேர்ச்சொல் means|root word|sentence|poem|Root.","s|What does சொல்வளம் mean?|word wealth|Wealth of words.","t|Many languages disappeared over time.|T|Yes."])
T(1,I1,"kaalakkanithan","Kaalakkanithan (காலக்கணிதம்) by Kannadasan",
 "A poet describes himself and what true poetry should stand for.",
 "Kaalakkanithan is a memorisation poem by the poet Kannadasan. The unit says that humanity is the clear essence of the way of life of an individual and society, and a good poet is the very grammar of humanity.",
 "A poet's mind says boldly what it thinks right, does not bow to wealth or office, and shares with others. The poem presents the poet as a reckoner of time who speaks truth.",
 "Terms: கவிஞன் (poet), மனிதம் (humanity), துணிவு (courage) and காலம் (time).",
 ["கவிஞன்","மனிதம்","துணிவு","காலம்","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("A good poet bows to power.",["He speaks truth boldly.","He does not bow to wealth."]),
 ["m|Kaalakkanithan is by|Kannadasan|Bharathidasan|Kamban|Kannadasan.","m|A good poet does not bow to|wealth or position|truth|kindness|He is bold.","t|The poem is for memorisation.|T|Yes.","m|காலம் means|time|place|colour|Time.","s|What does கவிஞன் mean?|poet|Poet.","t|The poet shares with others.|T|Yes."])
T(1,I1,"puyalile-oru-thoni","Puyalile Oru Thoni (புயலிலே ஒரு தோணி) by Pa. Singaram",
 "A small boat meets a mighty storm at sea.",
 "This is an extract from a novel by Pa. Singaram. When nature turns furious and becomes a dance of destruction, we are helpless. The story shows the great sight of a storm that threatens to roll up a ship at sea, and the struggle of a small boat.",
 "It shows the power of nature and the courage and skill of the sailors. The writer's vivid description makes the storm real to the reader.",
 "Terms: புயல் (storm), தோணி (boat), கடல் (sea) and இயற்கை சீற்றம் (nature's fury).",
 ["புயல்","தோணி","கடல்","சீற்றம்","புதினம்"],
 ("The story describes a calm sea.",["It describes a storm.","A small boat struggles."]),
 ["m|புயல் means|storm|boat|king|Storm.","m|தோணி means|boat|ship's captain|rock|Boat.","t|The extract is from a novel.|T|Yes.","m|The writer is|Pa. Singaram|Kannadasan|Kamban|Pa. Singaram.","s|What does கடல் mean?|sea|Sea.","t|It shows the fury of nature.|T|Yes."])
T(1,I1,"sol-grammar","Grammar: Word (சொல்)",
 "Words are the building blocks of every sentence.",
 "In Tamil grammar a சொல் (word) is classified into four kinds: பெயர்ச்சொல் (noun), வினைச்சொல் (verb), இடைச்சொல் (particle) and உரிச்சொல் (qualifier). Each has its own work in a sentence.",
 "Words can also be single words (தனிமொழி), compound words (தொடர்மொழி) or words with parts (பொதுமொழி). Learning these helps in analysis and in writing correctly.",
 "Practise by taking a sentence and naming each word's type. This textbook section is a general introduction; read the exact definitions in your book.",
 ["சொல்","பெயர்ச்சொல்","வினைச்சொல்","இடைச்சொல்","உரிச்சொல்"],
 ("There are only two kinds of words.",["There are four.","Noun, verb, particle and qualifier."]),
 ["m|பெயர்ச்சொல் is a|noun|verb|particle|Noun.","m|வினைச்சொல் is a|verb|noun|qualifier|Verb.","t|Tamil words are of four kinds.|T|Yes.","m|உரிச்சொல் is a|qualifier|noun|verb|Qualifier.","s|How many main kinds of words are there?|four;4|Four.","t|A சொல் means a word.|T|Yes."])
I2="Iyal 2: Nature, Environment and Science (இயற்கை, சுற்றுச்சூழல், அறிவியல்)"
T(2,I2,"ariviyal-ketkiratha","Ariviyal Ketkiratha en Kural! (அறிவியல் கேட்கிறதா என் குரல்!)",
 "Can anyone hear nature crying out about polluted air?",
 "This unit's learning goals include reading news about air pollution and discussing it, and enjoying Sangam songs and new poems that picture nature. The lesson raises the alarm about environmental damage and asks whether our voice is heard.",
 "It teaches that science should be used to protect nature, and that every person is responsible for reducing pollution.",
 "Terms: காற்று மாசுபாடு (air pollution), சுற்றுச்சூழல் (environment), அறிவியல் (science) and பாதுகாப்பு (protection).",
 ["மாசுபாடு","சுற்றுச்சூழல்","அறிவியல்","பாதுகாப்பு","காற்று"],
 ("Air pollution is not a problem.",["It is a serious problem.","We must protect nature."]),
 ["m|காற்று மாசுபாடு means|air pollution|water|sound|Air pollution.","m|சுற்றுச்சூழல் means|environment|school|temple|Environment.","t|Science can help protect nature.|T|Yes.","m|பாதுகாப்பு means|protection|danger|speed|Protection.","s|What does அறிவியல் mean?|science|Science.","t|Everyone shares the responsibility.|T|Yes."])
T(2,I2,"pariyaadal","Pariyaadal (பரிபாடல்) — a Sangam text",
 "A Sangam poem sings of the cosmos and its creation.",
 "Pariyaadal is one of the eight Sangam anthologies (எட்டுத்தொகை) and is sung in a special mixed metre called paripadal. The poem in the textbook describes the beginnings of the universe and natural features in a poetic way.",
 "It shows that ancient Tamils had a sense of the origin and order of nature. It is valued for its music and its picture of nature.",
 "Terms: பரிபாடல், எட்டுத்தொகை, சங்க இலக்கியம் and இசைப்பாடல் (musical poem).",
 ["பரிபாடல்","எட்டுத்தொகை","சங்க இலக்கியம்","இசைப்பாடல்","இயற்கை"],
 ("Pariyaadal is a modern novel.",["It is a Sangam text.","It is one of the eight anthologies."]),
 ["m|Pariyaadal belongs to|Ettuthokai|Ainperumkappiyam|Modern poems|Eight anthologies.","m|It is a|musical poem|play|dictionary|Sung poems.","t|It is a Sangam work.|T|Yes.","m|எட்டுத்தொகை means|eight anthologies|eight kings|eight roads|Eight collections.","s|What type of literature is Pariyaadal?|Sangam;சங்க இலக்கியம்|Sangam literature.","t|It describes nature.|T|Yes."])
T(2,I2,"megam","Megam (மேகம்) by Nagore Rumi",
 "A cloud is our roof, our beauty and our messenger.",
 "Megam is a new poem (புதுக்கவிதை) by Nagore Rumi. It says that the cloud is our roof and adorns the sky. Bharathi described the evening clouds beautifully, even forgetting metre, and poets have made the cloud a messenger, as in Kalidasa's Meghasandesham.",
 "The poem delights in the cloud's beauty and its role in bringing rain. It shows that nature inspires poets.",
 "Terms: மேகம் (cloud), புதுக்கவிதை (free verse), தூது (messenger) and அழகு (beauty).",
 ["மேகம்","புதுக்கவிதை","தூது","அழகு","வானம்"],
 ("The poem is a prose essay.",["It is a new poem.","The cloud is praised."]),
 ["m|Megam is by|Nagore Rumi|Kannadasan|Kamban|Nagore Rumi.","m|மேகம் means|cloud|river|sun|Cloud.","t|Poets made the cloud a messenger.|T|Yes.","m|புதுக்கவிதை is|free verse|epic|play|Modern poetry.","s|Which Sanskrit work sends a cloud as messenger?|Meghasandesham;மேகசந்தேசம்|Kalidasa's.","t|Bharathi described the evening clouds.|T|Yes."])
T(2,I2,"brahmmam","Brahmmam (பிரும்மம்) by Prabanjan",
 "Planting a tree and waiting for its first leaf is a lesson in love.",
 "Brahmmam is a short story by Prabanjan. It says that living with nature and making nature useful is true aesthetics, and that growing trees is one way of repaying nature's kindness. When a sapling grows into a tree, its first leaf, flower and fruit bring joy.",
 "The story presents tree planting as devotion and gratitude to nature.",
 "Terms: மரம் (tree), இயற்கை (nature), நன்றிக்கடன் (debt of gratitude) and சிறுகதை.",
 ["மரம்","இயற்கை","நன்றிக்கடன்","சிறுகதை","பிரபஞ்சன்"],
 ("The story is about a battle.",["It is about trees.","It teaches gratitude to nature."]),
 ["m|Brahmmam is by|Prabanjan|Pa. Singaram|Kannadasan|Prabanjan.","m|The story values|growing trees|building walls|fishing|Planting trees.","t|It is a short story.|T|Yes.","m|மரம் means|tree|house|cloud|Tree.","s|What does நன்றி mean?|gratitude;thanks|Thanks.","t|Trees repay nature's kindness.|T|Yes."])
T(2,I2,"thogaanilai-thodargal","Grammar: Thogaanilaith thodargal (தொகாநிலைத் தொடர்கள்)",
 "Words stand side by side with their meaning clear and nothing hidden.",
 "தொகாநிலைத் தொடர் is a phrase in which words are joined without any dropped (தொக்க) element. There are nine kinds: எழுவாய்த்தொடர், விளித்தொடர், வினைமுற்றுத்தொடர், பெயரெச்சத்தொடர், வினையெச்சத்தொடர், வேற்றுமைத்தொடர், இடைச்சொல்தொடர், உரிச்சொல்தொடர் and அடுக்குத்தொடர்.",
 "In each kind, the word relation is visible, for instance a subject followed by a verb, or a vocative followed by its sentence.",
 "Practise by identifying the type in sentences. Remember the contrast with தொகைநிலைத் தொடர், where a meaning-bearing word is hidden.",
 ["தொகாநிலைத்தொடர்","எழுவாய்த்தொடர்","விளித்தொடர்","அடுக்குத்தொடர்","வேற்றுமைத்தொடர்"],
 ("There are six kinds.",["There are nine.","No word is hidden."]),
 ["m|How many kinds of thogaanilai thodar?|Nine|Six|Three|Nine.","m|In thogaanilai thodar|nothing is hidden|a word is dropped|a letter is removed|No dropped element.","t|Vilith-thodar is a vocative phrase.|T|Yes.","m|Adukkuth-thodar is|a repeated word|a verb|a vowel|Repetition.","s|What does தொடர் mean?|phrase;sentence|A phrase.","t|It differs from thogai nilai.|T|Yes."])
